signee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4.1, 4.5.1, 4.6.1, 4.7-dev3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev3 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9579) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900HS with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.40 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nUsing MSDF changes the glyph size of a font (see below gif):\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d48972d-70fd-4ce9-8506-685eab268976)\n\nReproducible with multiple fonts (normal and monospaced), and also in Compatibility and Forwards+ renderers.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a Label with some text.\n2. Assign a FontFile via theme overrides.\n3. Reimport font with MSDF or toggle `multichannel_signed_distance_field` property of FontFile.\n4. Notice that the glyphs change in size.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP: [font-tests.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26557717/font-tests.zip)\n\nUse the provided tool button on root node to toggle MSDF on the attached `Roboto Mono` font.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizatio